G-DF-DEPLOY (DF-B6) — the harness mem_class CURATOR deploys the promoted 0.5B adapter as the
drop-in replacement for the engine's 12B model_classify. The self-improvement loop is CLOSED. (2026-07-03)
=========================================================================================
Deployment choice (operator-confirmed): the HARNESS CURATOR. ADR-002 idle-vs-hot-path discipline —
classification is an OFFLINE Tier-1 DECIDER, so it lives where the PyTorch adapter lives (the
harness), NOT in the resident engine's VRAM/loop. It emits a clean symbolic label (mem_class) into
the shared store; the engine EXECUTES it by hot-reloading via the LM-B1 reconciler (already GREEN).
Mirrors the NIGHTSHIFT precedent (background work in the background). Reuses the EXACT DF-B3/B4
artifact; zero engine rebuild.

BUILD (harness, this-commit):
  * datagen/mem_class_curator.py: MemClassCurator loads the promoted adapter (base Qwen2.5-0.5B +
    LoRA) on CPU (CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES forced empty — never touches the engine GPU). classify(stmt)
    = same PROMPT/parser as train/eval. curate_store(root) = the model_classify replacement: for
    each memory-okf/full/<addr>.md, classify the body; if it differs from the frontmatter mem_class
    (and safety-monotone allows), rewrite the policy lines (Python mirror of engine rewrite_okf_class).
    active_adapter() resolves the promoted repo from datagen/model_registry.json (DF-B4).
  * run_agency.py _start_mem_curator(): loads the curator once on a background thread + re-curates
    the store every SP_MEM_CURATOR_SEC. Gated SP_MEM_CURATOR=1 (default off), SP_MEM_CURATOR_ROOT,
    SP_MEM_CURATOR_ADAPTER. Load/pass failures caught — never breaks agency.

GATE G-DF-DEPLOY (CPU, in the harness):
  * curator loaded on CPU (no GPU).
  * CPU classify acc on the DISTINCT eval set = 25/30 = 0.833 — reproduces DF-B4 exactly, proving the
